          "author": "hsluoyz",
          "created_at": "2026-10-23T10:26:38Z",
          "classification": "UPSTREAM_FIX_ANNOUNCEMENT_NOT_REPLY_TO_NAIF",
          "body": "Thanks for the detailed report. Fixed in https://github.com/casdoor/casdoor/commit/20245fbdb7dd62823d164ad6dbdc0596f7df0cca\n\n- CIMD now accepts `token_endpoint_auth_method: private_key_jwt`, so ChatGPT's https://chatgpt.com/oauth/client.json is no longer rejected.\n- For DCR and CIMD clients that use `private_key_jwt`, Casdoor stores the client's `jwks_uri` and verifies `client_assertion` at the token endpoint per RFC 7523: signature against the client's JWKS, `iss` and `sub` equal to the client_id, `aud` is the token endpoint or the issuer, and `exp` is required.\n- DCR now rejects `token_endpoint_auth_method` values that Casdoor doesn't support, and `private_key_jwt` without an https `jwks_uri`, instead of returning 201 for a client that can never get a token.\n"
        }
      ],
